{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Motivation","text":"Motivation","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Natural language date input features can be found in apps like "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/culturedcode.com\/things\/support\/articles\/9780167\/","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/flexibits.com\/fantastical-ios\/help\/adding","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.raycast.com\/extensions\/reminders","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and make the user experience better."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Usage","text":"Usage","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SoulverCore"},{"type":"text","text":" adds a single property "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dateValue"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public extension String {","   var dateValue: Date?","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this property to extract the last natural language date found in the string. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dateValue"},{"type":"text","text":" will be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" if there are no dates in the string."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"SoulverCore-vs-Foundations-DataDetector","text":"SoulverCore vs Foundation’s DataDetector","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apple’s Foundation framework includes NSDataDetector for detecting dates in strings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is an example:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let expression = \"March 5th, 2023\"","let types: NSTextCheckingResult.CheckingType = [.date ]","let detector = try! NSDataDetector(types: types.rawValue)","let match = detector.matches(in: expression, options: .init(rawValue: 0), range: NSRange(location: 0, length: expression.count)).first","let date = match?.date"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Compare this to SoulverCore:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let date = \"March 5th, 2023\".dateValue"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to a much nicer API, SoulverCore also adds a number of additional features not supported by NSDataDetector."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Supported-Features","text":"Supported Features","type":"heading"},{"level":4,"anchor":"Natural-language-calendar-math","text":"Natural language calendar math","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use natural language phrases like “3 weeks from tomorrow” and “march 12 + 4 weeks 3 days”."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SoulverCore supports a large range of different natural language date syntaxes. See the "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/documentation.soulver.app\/syntax-reference\/dates-and-times","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for more examples."}]},{"level":4,"anchor":"Units--unit-shorthands","text":"Units & unit shorthands","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SoulverCore interprets units of time as referring to a future date after the specified amount of time has passed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2 weeks 2 days"},{"type":"text","text":" will be interpreted as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2 weeks and 2 days"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"from now","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following time unit shorthands are also supported:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“1y” (1 year)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“5mo” (5 months)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“3w” (3 weeks)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“2d” (2 days)"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shorthands can be combined together:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“12-9 9p” means the “12th of September at 9pm” (in a non-US locale)"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":4,"anchor":"Half-formed-dates","text":"Half-formed dates","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Examples:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“3\/12” (Dec 3, or March 12 in the US)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“12.2” (Feb 12 or Dec 2 in the US)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“9-5” (May 9 or Sep 5 in the US)"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":4,"anchor":"Day--month-shorthands","text":"Day & month shorthands","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Examples:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Next mon” (next monday)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“tod” (today)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“apr3” (April 3)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“yes” (yesterday)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“tom” (tomorrow)"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":4,"anchor":"AMPM-shorthands","text":"AM\/PM shorthands","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Examples:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“3p” (3pm)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“5a” (5am)"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":4,"anchor":"Random-words-ignored","text":"Random words ignored","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SoulverCore extracts the last date present in the given string, and ignores random words before and after it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, the following are valid inputs:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Tom’s birthday party "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"this sunday","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"”"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Schedule the meeting for "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"April 21st next year","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"”"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"June 5","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the kids get off school”"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Detailed-information-about-the-parsed-date","text":"Detailed information about the parsed date","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/app.soulver.core\/documentation\/SoulverCore\/Datestamp\/DatestampType","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" enum contains detailed information about the kind of date detected and what date components were explicitly specified."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is how an example of how to get the formatting and components of the detected date:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var engineCustomization = EngineCustomization.standard","engineCustomization.featureFlags.seeksFutureDate = true","let calculator = Calculator(customization: engineCustomization)","","if let datestampType = calculator.dateFor(inputDateText)?.result.evaluationResult.datestampValue?.type {","    print(\"Date of type \\(datestampType)\")","}"]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Performance","text":"Performance","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SoulverCore is very efficient and can perform thousands of date-from-string extractions every second."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Localizations","text":"Localizations","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to English, SoulverCore is localized into German, French, Spanish, Russian & Simplified Chinese."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The user’s system locale will be used for date parsing, and date & time formats specific the particular region are taken into account."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/app.soulver.core\/documentation\/SoulverCore\/ObjectParsing","doc:\/\/app.soulver.core\/documentation\/SoulverCore\/DataParsing"],"anchor":"Data-Parsing","title":"Data Parsing","generated":true}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"SoulverCore"}],"title":"Dates from strings"},"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/soulvercore\/dateparsing"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/app.soulver.core\/documentation\/SoulverCore\/DateParsing"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/app.soulver.core\/documentation\/SoulverCore"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Add a natural language date scheduling feature to your Mac or iOS calendar or reminders app","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://app.soulver.core/documentation/SoulverCore/Datestamp/DatestampType":{"url":"\/documentation\/soulvercore\/datestamp\/datestamptype","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DatestampType"}],"title":"Datestamp.DatestampType","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The types of datestamps supported by SoulverCore"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/app.soulver.core\/documentation\/SoulverCore\/Datestamp\/DatestampType","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DatestampType"}]},"https://www.raycast.com/extensions/reminders":{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.raycast.com\/extensions\/reminders","type":"link","title":"Raycast","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Raycast"}],"url":"https:\/\/www.raycast.com\/extensions\/reminders"},"doc://app.soulver.core/documentation/SoulverCore":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A powerful natural language calculation engine"}],"title":"SoulverCore","url":"\/documentation\/soulvercore","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/app.soulver.core\/documentation\/SoulverCore"},"https://culturedcode.com/things/support/articles/9780167/":{"titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Things","type":"text"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/culturedcode.com\/things\/support\/articles\/9780167\/","title":"Things","url":"https:\/\/culturedcode.com\/things\/support\/articles\/9780167\/"},"https://flexibits.com/fantastical-ios/help/adding":{"url":"https:\/\/flexibits.com\/fantastical-ios\/help\/adding","identifier":"https:\/\/flexibits.com\/fantastical-ios\/help\/adding","type":"link","title":"Fantastical","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fantastical"}]},"doc://app.soulver.core/documentation/SoulverCore/ObjectParsing":{"type":"topic","title":"Objects from strings","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/app.soulver.core\/documentation\/SoulverCore\/ObjectParsing","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Transform natural language strings into strongly-typed Swift objects with a single call"}],"url":"\/documentation\/soulvercore\/objectparsing"},"doc://app.soulver.core/documentation/SoulverCore/DataParsing":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/soulvercore\/dataparsing","title":"Data from strings","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/app.soulver.core\/documentation\/SoulverCore\/DataParsing","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"A declarative & type-safe approach to extracting various data types out of strings","type":"text"}]},"https://documentation.soulver.app/syntax-reference/dates-and-times":{"identifier":"https:\/\/documentation.soulver.app\/syntax-reference\/dates-and-times","type":"link","title":"Soulver Documentation","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Soulver Documentation"}],"url":"https:\/\/documentation.soulver.app\/syntax-reference\/dates-and-times"}}}